* @coreweave/docs

# Code owners for the CoreWeave skills library.
#
# These paths decide which remote code runs on a customer's cluster, or can
# switch off a check that guards it. Changes to them request review from the
# team that owns them.
#
# The catch-all above ensures every file is owned. Specific rules below take
# precedence because GitHub uses the last matching rule.

# --- Pinned dependencies ----------------------------------------------------
# These hold the commit SHA, chart versions, and release pin that decide which
# remote code runs under the customer's own credentials. Reviewing a bump means
# reading the UPSTREAM diff, not the changed pin line: see CONTRIBUTING.md,
# "Pinned dependencies".
/_snippets/coreweave-cks.md                                    @coreweave/docs
/skills/cw-self-managed-inference/body.md                      @coreweave/docs
/skills/cw-load-model-to-bucket/references/s3-client-setup.md  @coreweave/docs

# The automation that proposes those bumps. Loosen a regex here and the pins
# silently stop being proposed — no error, just nothing.
/.github/renovate.json5                                        @coreweave/docs

# --- The gates themselves ---------------------------------------------------
# Whatever can switch a check off is owned alongside the check. Every script
# here is stdlib-only; the first two run in build.yml, the third in
# eval-hygiene.yml.
/.github/workflows/                                            @coreweave/docs
/scripts/check_pinned_deps.py                                  @coreweave/docs
/scripts/lint_skill_content.py                                 @coreweave/docs
/scripts/check_eval_hygiene_selftest.py                        @coreweave/docs

# The eval hygiene gate (APPSEC-3971). The allowlist is listed for a reason the
# other gates don't have: it is DATA the scanner reads, so a PR that adds a leak
# can suppress its own finding by appending one regex, without touching a line
# of gate code. That is the specific hole evals/HYGIENE.md ("Gate integrity")
# names, and these two lines are what closes it.
/evals/check_eval_hygiene.py                                   @coreweave/docs
/evals/hygiene-allowlist.txt                                   @coreweave/docs

# --- The eval corpora themselves --------------------------------------------
# Distinct from the gate surfaces above, and owned by a wider set on purpose.
# The hygiene scanner is pattern-only: it catches identifiers that have a
# SHAPE, and structurally cannot catch a customer's NAME sitting in otherwise
# clean prose, or a fingerprint like a one-of-a-kind GPU mix that identifies an
# account without naming it. That needs a human who would recognize the
# account, which is why solutions-architecture is here alongside docs.
#
# Two owners on one line means EITHER satisfies the requirement — GitHub asks
# for approval from at least one listed owner, not all of them. Do not split
# these onto separate lines; the later line would win outright and silence the
# other group.
/evals/trigger-evals.jsonl                                     @coreweave/docs @coreweave/solutions-architecture
/skills/*/evals/                                               @coreweave/docs @coreweave/solutions-architecture
